    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38070" root="لوب" body-key="l">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَسْوَدُ لُوبِىٌّ</span></b>  (and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نُوبِىٌّ</span>, TA,) [<i>Very black</i>]:
derived from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُوبَةٌ</span>, as signifying “ a tract covered,
or strewed, with black stones ”: (K:) or from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اللُّوبُ</span> as a syn. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">النُّوبُ</span>, meaning [“ the
Nubians, ” but see above] “ a certain race, or nation,
of the negroes. ” (RA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُوبىٌّ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لُوبَةٌ</span>.

